<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heitersheim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heitersheim is a small town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/markgraflerland">Markgräflerland</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freiburg-im-breisgau">Freiburg im Breisgau</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> held it from the 13th century, and from 1505 it was the seat of their Grand Prior of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, who ruled it as a small principality of the Empire until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> annexed it in 1806. The priors' castle survives, and a large Roman villa has been excavated nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heitersheim.jpg" alt="Heitersheim" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rauenstein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heitersheim,_Rathaus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
